lation</article-title><source>Annu. Rev. Biochem.</source><volume>61</volume><year>1992</year><fpage>721</fpage><lpage>759</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1497323</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Tangetal1998"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tang</surname><given-names>H.</given-names></name><name><surname>Kerins</surname><given-names>D.M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Hao</surname><given-names>Q.</given-names></name><name><surname>Inagami</surname><given-names>T.</given-names></name><name><surname>Vaughan</surname><given-names>D.E.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The urokinase-type plasminogen activator receptor mediates tyrosine phosphorylation of focal adhesion proteins and activation of mitogen-activated protein kinase in cultured endothelial cells</article-title><source>J. Biol. Chem.</source><volume>273</volume><year>1998</year><fpage>18268</fpage><lpage>18272</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9660790</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Tkachuketal1996"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tkachuk</surname><given-names>V.</given-names></name><name><surname>Stepanova</surname><given-names>V.</given-names></name><name><surname>Little</surname><given-names>P.J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Bobik</surname><given-names>A.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Regulation of urokinase plasminogen activator in vascular remodelling</article-title><source>Clin. Exp. Pharmacol. Physiol.</source><volume>23</volume><year>1996</year><fpage>759</fpage><lpage>765</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8911711</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="TsuboiandRifkin1990"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tsuboi</surname><given-names>R.</given-names></name><name><surname>Rifkin</surname><given-names>D.B.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Biomodal relationship between invasion of the amniotic membrane and plasminogen activator activity</article-title><source>Int. J. Cancer.</source><volume>46</volume><year>1990</year><fpage>56</fpage><lpage>60</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2142142</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Wangetal1997"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Mazar</surname><given-names>A.</given-names></name><name><surname>Quan</surname><given-names>N.</given-names></name><name><surname>Schneider</surname><given-names>A.</given-names></name><name><surname>Henkin</surname><given-names>J.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Plasminogen activation by pro-urokinase in complex with its receptor</article-title><source>Eur. J. Biochem.</source><volume>247</volume><year>1997</year><fpage>256</fpage><lpage>261</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9249034</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Weaveretal1997"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Weaver</surname><given-names>A.M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Hussaini</surname><given-names>I.M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Mazar</surname><given-names>A.</given-names></name><name><surname>Henkin</surname><given-names>J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Gonias</surname><given-names>S.L.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Embryonic fibroblasts that are deficient in low density lipoprotein receptor-related protein demonstrate increased activity of the urokinase receptor system and accelerated migration on vitronectin</article-title><source>J. Biol. Chem.</source><volume>272</volume><year>1997</year><fpage>14372</fpage><lpage>14379</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9162074</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Webbetal1999"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Webb</surname><given-names>D.J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Nguyen</surn